note count_trap3_wrap: off + n is never formed, so it cannot wrap: off 2^64-1 and n 2 would sum to 1,
note inside a 16-byte array, but off > len A - n, so count traps 3, exit 103
om2
text before "before\n"
fn main to int
k = write 1 before 0 len before
a = new uchar 16 10
o = ulong 18446744073709551615
n = count a o 2 10
ret int n
end
